munity based ambulator with umbrella as a cane. Tracing back her history, she had been having left foot drop since about 2019 before the BADLs were totally independent. She lives on the 2nd floor with husband and daughter.&nbsp;</p><p _ngcontent-ng-c2173368651="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted" style="color: rgb(31, 31, 31); font-family: &quot;Google Sans Flex&quot;, &quot;Google Sans&quot;, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-variant-ligatures: none; background-color: rgb(233, 238, 246);"><br></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c2173368651="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted" style="color: rgb(31, 31, 31); font-family: &quot;Google Sans Flex&quot;, &quot;Google Sans&quot;, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-variant-ligatures: none; background-color: rgb(233, 238, 246);">This time, at around 6am on 2026/05/05, she experienced sudden onset right side weakness at 04:00 upon waking up. She then presented to our emergency department, she was given 300 mg aspirin, and she felt better and was discharged at 13:50. However, at around 6am on 2026/05/06, progressive right-sided weakness, slurred speech, facial palsy and a fall were noted by her husband. She was brought to the ER again. Vitals showed hypertensive (BP 216/90 mmHg). Foley&nbsp;<span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-family: ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif, &quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;, &quot;Noto Color Emoji&quot;; font-size: 16px;">and NG tube&nbsp;</span><span style="background-color: rgb(233, 238, 246); color: rgb(31, 31, 31); font-family: &quot;Google Sans Flex&quot;, &quot;Google Sans&quot;, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 16px;">were indwelled. Brain CT showed hypoattenuation at the left central pons. DAPT with aspirin and clopidogrel with piracetam were given. She was then admitted to the neurological ward under the impression of acute ischemic stroke. On 2026/05/07, a brain MRI showed left medial pontine infarction. Duplex showed homogenous plaques in bilateral CCA, ICA, and ECA with high flow velocitty in the left ECA.&nbsp;</span><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-family: ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif, &quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;, &quot;Noto Color Emoji&quot;; font-size: 16px;">Foley catheter was removed on 2026/05/12 with smooth voiding.</span></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c2173368651="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted" style="color: rgb(31, 31, 31); font-family: &quot;Google Sans Flex&quot;, &quot;Google Sans&quot;, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-variant-ligatures: none; background-color: rgb(233, 238, 246);"><span style="background-color: rgb(233, 238, 246); color: rgb(31, 31, 31); font-family: &quot;Google Sans Flex&quot;, &quot;Google Sans&quot;, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 16px;"><br></span></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c2173368651="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted" style="background-color: rgb(233, 238, 246);"><span style="color: rgb(31, 31, 31); font-family: &quot;Google Sans Flex&quot;, &quot;Google Sans&quot;, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-variant-ligatures: none; background-color: rgb(233, 238, 246);">In terms of neurological recovery, right hemiplegia (MMT 2) was noted upon admission. The first physiatrist consultaiton was made on 2026/05/07, by which her motor status had not gained much improvement, the&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(31, 31, 31); font-family: ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif, &quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;, &quot;Noto Color Emoji&quot;; font-size: 16px; font-variant-ligatures: none; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">Brunnstrom Stage was III over the right side.</span><span style="color: rgb(31, 31, 31); font-family: &quot;Google Sans Flex&quot;, &